\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0\qc {\f1\fs120\cf1 How the World Became Rich\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0\qc {\i0\f1\fs46\cf2 Chapter 9\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0\qc {\i0\f1\fs46\cf2 The Rise of the Modern Economy\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 The Fruits of Industrialization\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 The Industrial Revolution did not transform the lives of workers in a single generation\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Due to rapid population growth and ongoing war (usually with France), British real wage growth lagged\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 GDP per capita increased but many workers did not see major improvements in living standards, at least until after around 1840\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Allen (2009) labeled this \'93Engle\'92s Pause\'94\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 But from the 1840s onwards there was a decisive increase in both per capita GDP and real wages\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 Consequences of Industrialization\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Industrialization led to much pessimism about the state of the working class\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Karl Marx was the most famous proponent of the \'93pessimistic case\'94\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Urban crowding \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Increased coal pollution\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 Thomas Babington Macaulay's Optimism \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Macaulay was one of the first individuals to understand the consequences of the Industrial Revolution\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 He predicted that modern economic growth would transform both England and the world\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 He was proven correct\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 The Second Industrial Revolution\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Many of the innovations of the First Industrial Revolution did not rely directly on scientific breakthroughs\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 After 1850, however, innovations in chemistry, medicine, and physics started to have direct economic payoffs\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 This was the \'93marriage of science and technology\'94\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\i0\f1\cf1 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 The Demographic Transition\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 A key reason why per capita incomes increased during the 2}{\i0\f1\super\cf1 nd}{\i0\f1\cf1  Industrial Revolution was that demographic behavior changed\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Beginning with France (and then later in England), people started to control fertility within marriage\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 This demographic transition meant that economies stopped behaving in a Malthusian fashion\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Population growth slowed even as incomes improved\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 The Demographic Transition\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 The timing of the fertility transition is hard to explain\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 It began in France in the late 18}{\i0\f1\super\cf1 th}{\i0\f1\cf1  century, before the onset of modern economic growth\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Spolaore}{\i0\f1\cf1  and }{\i0\f1\cf1 Wacziarg}{\i0\f1\cf1  (2021) argue that it diffused alongside French culture in the 19}{\i0\f1\super\cf1 th}{\i0\f1\cf1  century\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 As Malthusian pressures eased, resources were freed up to invest in education\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 Human Capital and the Demographic Transition\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Gary Becker argued that parents choose between the quality and quantity of children\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 After the demographic transition, societies moved along a quantity-quality trade-off, investing more in education\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 An educated labor force was a key complement to the technologies of the Second Industrial Revolution\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\i0\f1\cf1 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 Late Industrializers\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 The key insight of Alexander }{\i0\f1\cf1 Gershenrkon}{\i0\f1\cf1  was that later industrializers did not have to go through the same steps as Britain\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Early stages of development could be leap-frogged\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Late industrializers had a backlog of advanced technologies they could adopt\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Germany harnessed capital on a larger scale (via investment banks) than Britain had ever done, becoming a leader in new sectors such as chemical fertilizers (Bayer, IG Farben) and arms (Krupp) \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 Human Capital and the Diffusion of Industrialization\line \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Human capital played a critical role in the diffusion of industrialization and in the Second Industrial Revolution\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Becker et al. (2011) document this by studying regional variation in industrialization within Germany in the late 19}{\i0\f1\super\cf1 th}{\i0\f1\cf1  century\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 They main finding is that pre-industrial levels of education (measured in 1816) predict which locations industrialized in the second part of the 19th century\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 They show that education was associated with non-textile-based industrialization\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\i0\f1\cf1 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 Human Capital and the Diffusion of Industrialization\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 The effects of education were strongest on non-textiles and non-metal based industrialization\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 There was no effect on textile industries (which required less human capital)\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\i0\f1\cf1 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 The Economic Rise of the USA\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 The United States became the world\'92s leading economy by the end of the 19}{\i0\f1\super\cf1 th}{\i0\f1\cf1  century\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\i0\f1\cf1 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 The Economic Rise of the USA\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 The Economic Rise of the USA\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 The First Industrial Revolution (1760-1830)\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li2160\fi-605\kerning24\lang1033\li1440 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \'96\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'96}}{\f1\fs40\cf1 Began in England, spread to USA & Belgium in 1820s, Germany in the 1840s-1850s\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li2160\fi-605\kerning24\lang1033\li1440 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \'96\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'96}}{\f1\fs40\cf1 Key technologies: cotton textiles, steam engine, iron & steel\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Industrialization began in New England\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li2160\fi-605\kerning24\lang1033\li1440 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \'96\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'96}}{\f1\fs40\cf1 The Beverly Cotton Manufactory in Massachusetts in 1787\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li2160\fi-605\kerning24\lang1033\li1440 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \'96\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'96}}{\f1\fs40\cf1 Slater Mill in Rhode Island in 1790 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li2160\fi-605\kerning24\lang1033\li1440 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \'96\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'96}}{\f1\fs40\cf1 Waltham Mill in Massachusetts in 1814\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li2160\fi-605\kerning24\lang1033\li1440 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \'96\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'96}}{\f1\fs40\cf1 Timber, water, coal, iron, copper were abundant\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li2160\fi-605\kerning24\lang1033\li1440 {\f1\fs40\cf1 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\i0\f1\cf1 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 Cotton and Textiles\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\i0\f1\cf1 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Industrialization in the first half of the 19th century centered on cotton\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 America was a technological follower\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Rapid growth was possible due to abundance of cheap factor inputs\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs80\cf1 The Diffusion of Technology from Britain to Europe & N. America (Allen\'92s interpretation)\line \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Recall the argument of Allen (2009): factor prices determine patterns of innovation\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Countries with factor prices similar to Britain should have industrialized next\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 North America had expensive labor and abundant natural resources. High cost of labor provided the incentive to innovate\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s3\li2160\fi-605\kerning24\lang1033\li1440 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \'96\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \'96}}{\f1\fs40\cf1 For example, The first automatic flour mill invented by Oliver Evans in 1782\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Belgium, the first European country to industrialize, had abundant coal\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\i0\f1\cf1 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs80\cf1 The Diffusion of Technology from Britain to Europe & N. America (Mokyr\'92s interpretation)}{\f1\fs72\cf1 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Recall the argument of Mokyr (2009, 2016): a culture of growth or the Industrial Enlightenment was critical for the onset of economic growth\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 America and Britain shared a common language and culture\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Despite attempts to restrict the spread of industrial revolution technologies to North America, this proved impossible\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Economic growth diffused first to Northern European societies that had participated in the Enlightenment and the Scientific Revolution\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 The Rise of the United States\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 America\'92s growth in the 19}{\i0\f1\super\cf1 th}{\i0\f1\cf1  century was also on the extensive margin\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Vast swathes of land were added and the population increased from around 2.5 million in 1776 to 76 million in 1900\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Immigration (especially from Ireland, Germany, Italy, and Eastern Europe) fueled this expansion\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 This expansion in the size of the market complemented a distinctively \'93American\'94 system of manufacturing\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 The Second Industrial Revolution and American Economic Growth\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 The American system of manufacturing centered on machine tools and the development of interchangeable parts\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 A large market and homogeneous tastes encouraged product standardization\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Standardized products could be easily tweaked or improved upon\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Standardized products encouraged the standardization of other parts, and this made further innovation easier\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 America became the leader in global manufacturing and in technology (though not necessarily in science until WWII)\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\i0\f1\cf1 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 The Soviet Detour I\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 In the 20}{\i0\f1\super\cf1 th}{\i0\f1\cf1  century the Soviet Union was seen as pioneering an alternative growth model to that of the United States or Western Europe\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 The Soviet Union achieved rapid industrialization in the 1930s (at vast human cost including millions of deaths in Ukraine due to famine) and fast growth for several decades\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 This was interpreted as due to the success of economic planning\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\i0\f1\cf1 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 The Soviet Detour II\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Russia under the Tsars was a rapidly growing and industrializing economy, on course to achieve rapid catch-up growth and industrialization prior to WWI\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Much of the early Soviet growth was recovery from the devastation the Russian economy experienced in WWI and during the Russian civil war\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 This growth was largely achieved by mobilizing tremendous resources (labor, land, natural resources, and physical capital)\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\i0\f1\cf1 \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 The Soviet Detour III\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Planning mobilized resources on a large scale but at tremendous costs\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Even during the early phase of rapid growth, inefficiencies and wastage were legendary (Gregory and Harrison, 2005). The price system existed to allocate scarce resources. Soviet planners struggled to \'93price\'94 intermediate goods  \par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Centralization of all economic decisions in the hands of a dictator produced chaos. Stalin spent his time making seemingly trivial decisions, including setting the price of metro tickets and making detailed managerial appointments (Gregory, 2004a, pp. 112\'9614)\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Corruption and rent-seeking were endemic\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 There were reforms after the death of Stalin. But after the 1950s, the USSR struggled to provide basic consumer goods that people wished to buy\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s1\li605\fi-605\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li0\fi0 {\f1\fs88\cf1 Chapter Summary\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Industrialization took several decades to significantly raise living standards in Britain and to spread to other parts of the world\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 The demographic transition at the end of the 19}{\i0\f1\super\cf1 th}{\i0\f1\cf1  century accelerated economic growth as did the transformative technologies of the Second Industrial Revolution such as electricity, chemical fertilizers, and the automobile engine\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 Human capital became more important for growth during this era\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 The United States was the fastest growing economy in the second half of the 19}{\i0\f1\super\cf1 th}{\i0\f1\cf1  century, taking a lead in the new technologies of the period\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 In particular, the United States pioneered the development of machine tools and mass production, which in the 20}{\i0\f1\super\cf1 th}{\i0\f1\cf1  century were epitomize by Frederick Taylor and Henry Ford\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs40 \uc1\u9632\'a6\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnfs40{\pntxtb \uc1\u9632\'a6}}{\i0\f1\cf1 The Soviet Union pioneered a different path towards modern economic growth. }{\i0\f1\cf1 It was }{\i0\f1\cf1 one that came at great human cost and ultimately failed\par 
}\pard\plain\ltrpar\s2\li1440\fi-605\i\kerning24\fs40\lang1033\li605 {\i0\f1\cf1 \par 
}
}